<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh industry output rises 2.6 pct in Jan-May.</title>
<headline>Kazakh industry output rises 2.6 pct in Jan-May.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kazakhstan's industrial output grew by 2.6 percent in January-May of this year, compared to the same period last year, the National Statistics Agency said on Thursday.</p>
<p>    KAZAKH INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT	 Jan-May '97	Jan-May '96</p>
<p>    Year-on-year pct change	     +2.6		 +0.4</p>
<p>The agency estimated the Central Asian state's industrial production in the first five months of this year at 326.5 billion tenge, compared to 304.5 billion tenge in the same period last year.</p>
<p>($1 = 75.5380 tenge)</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
